# GEOFUSION — Supabase Environment Variables
#
# DIAGNOSIS (2026-08-13):
#   The previous content of this file was a short-lived ES256-signed user-session JWT
#   (alg: ES256, aud: "authenticated", exp: 2026-08-13T16:55:36). That is a GoTrue user
#   session token — it is NOT a Supabase API key and will never work as one.
#
# WHAT IS NEEDED:
#   Supabase REST API (PostgREST) requires HS256-signed static JWTs issued at project creation.
#   There are two: the `anon` key (public, safe to commit) and the `service_role` key (secret).
#
# HOW TO FIX:
#   1. Go to: https://supabase.com/dashboard/project/cxbnxqvpyansdabjteuv/settings/api
#   2. Copy "Project API keys" → anon (public)   → paste as SUPABASE_ANON_KEY below
#   3. Copy "Project API keys" → service_role     → paste as SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY below
#   4. The JWT secret shown under "JWT Settings" should match what PostgREST uses. No action
#      needed there unless you've rotated it — but DO verify it matches if 401s persist.
#
# NOTE: pipeline_common.py uses SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY for ETL writes.
#       export_training_data.py uses the direct Postgres URL (bypasses PostgREST) for bulk reads.

SUPABASE_URL=https://cxbnxqvpyansdabjteuv.supabase.co

# Paste the `anon` key from the dashboard (Settings > API > Project API keys > anon):
SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9.eyJpc3MiOiJzdXBhYmFzZSIsInJlZiI6ImN4Ym54cXZweWFuc2RhYmp0ZXV2Iiwicm9sZSI6ImFub24iLCJpYXQiOjE3ODY2MDI3MDcsImV4cCI6MjEwMjE3ODcwN30._nnU1nvmUjU3PciNZZhTxAyUA7tz-GvRcX6fsgW_exs

